§ `s 54, ss 13(3), 59A -- may I claim, and whose permission do I need`

-- k053: Jake, Ruby's father, unmarried: s 54(1)(c) lets him claim as a parent who is not the birth mother; he needs Tahlia's permission.
#ASSERT `May I make a PPL claim` `a parent who is not the birth mother` FALSE

#ASSERT `Do I need the birth mother's permission` `a parent who is not the birth mother`

-- c063: Liam's 20 days need Chloe's permission for at least 20 days, and Chloe to have satisfied the work test.
#ASSERT `Does the birth mother let me be paid for these days` `the partner of the birth mother` TRUE TRUE 20 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the birth mother let me be paid for these days` `the partner of the birth mother` FALSE TRUE 20 20)

§ `s 11D, ss 31AB, 31ABA -- how many days`

#ASSERT NOT (`Is the day a flexible PPL day for my child` 20300905 20320905)

-- c061 (Oliver, 5 Sep 2030), c071 (Ella, 12 Apr 2033), d040 (Luca, 2 Feb 2030): 130 days, not the 24 weeks (120) c061 expects.
#ASSERT `How many days can be paid for my child` 20300905 EQUALS 130
#ASSERT `How many days can be paid for my child` 20330412 EQUALS 130

#ASSERT `What is the most days I can be paid when partnered` 20300905 EQUALS 110

#ASSERT `How many days are reserved for the other parent` 20300905 EQUALS 20

-- c061: 26 weeks in all; 22 for Chloe; 4 reserved (matching c061's 4).
#ASSERT `in weeks of five week days` 130 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `in weeks of five week days` 20 EQUALS 4

-- c061 Chloe partnered, nothing paid yet: 110. c063 Liam after Chloe's 110: 20. d040 Daniel after Priya's 110: 20.
-- A partnered parent experiencing family violence (PPL rules s 21(4)): the whole 130.
#ASSERT `How many more days can I be paid` 20300905 0 0 TRUE `none of them` EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `How many more days can I be paid` 20300905 110 0 TRUE `none of them` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `How many more days can I be paid` 20300202 110 0 TRUE `none of them` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `How many more days can I be paid` 20300905 0 0 TRUE `I am experiencing family and domestic violence or its impacts` EQUALS 130

§ `s 21; PPL rules s 7B -- days paid to both of us`

-- c063: Liam's four weeks alongside Chloe reach the 20 shared days exactly; a 21st shared day is barred.
#ASSERT `How many days can we both be paid for at once` 20300905 EQUALS 20

#ASSERT `May I be paid for a shared day` 20300905 19 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be paid for a shared day` 20300905 20 TRUE)

#ASSERT NOT (`Does a shared day count toward the limit` `a caesarean delivery, or a complication for the birth mother from the birth`)

§ `s 31AA -- am I eligible on the day`

-- k052: Tahlia is eligible married or not. k053: Jake loses a day he works three hours (s 31AA(2)(c)).
-- PPL rules ss 9(3)(b)(ii), 14: a parent may work while the baby is in hospital. d040: if Luca's birth day fell in Priya's
-- waiting period with no exemption on that day, becoming a citizen later does not help (s 31AA(2)(e)(ii)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible on the day` `Tahlia, unmarried, at home with Ruby` 130
#ASSERT `Am I eligible on the day` `Tahlia, had she been married` 130
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible on the day` `Jake, sole trader, working three hours that day` 20)
#ASSERT `Am I eligible on the day` `Jake, sole trader, not working that day` 20
#ASSERT `Am I eligible on the day` `a parent back at work while the baby is in hospital` 50
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible on the day` `a parent back at work with no PPL rules reason` 50)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I eligible on the day` `Priya in August 2030, Luca's birth day in her waiting period` 110)
#ASSERT `Am I eligible on the day` `Priya, had her waiting period ended before Luca was born` 110

§ `ss 32-36AA -- the work test`

-- c061: Chloe passes. k053: Jake passes on his own business. A partner cannot rely on pregnancy complications (s 36A(1)(a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy the work test` `the birth mother` `Chloe, six years at Ironbark`
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy the work test` `a parent who is not the birth mother` `Jake, riding for himself all year`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I satisfy the work test` `the birth mother` `a casual whose run is 294 days`)
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy the work test` `the birth mother` `pregnancy complications stopped work, the Secretary satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I satisfy the work test` `the partner of the birth mother` `pregnancy complications stopped work, the Secretary satisfied`)
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy the work test` `the partner of the birth mother` `a premature birth, the Secretary satisfied`

#ASSERT `Which day does my work test period run back from` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the expected date of birth`

#ASSERT NOT (`Is the gap a permissible break` 85)

§ `ss 34, 35, 35A; PPL rules ss 22, 23 -- qualifying work and paid work`

-- k053: Jake's riding is paid work under s 35(1) and (3). Working for one's own company still counts through s 35(3).
#ASSERT `Do I perform paid work` `Jake riding deliveries under his ABN`
#ASSERT `Do I perform paid work` `working as the employee of my own trading company`
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I perform paid work` `volunteering for an honorarium`)

#ASSERT `Is the day a qualifying work day` 0 0 8 FALSE

#ASSERT `How many hours does a PPL day for an earlier child count for` 0 EQUALS 7.6

§ `ss 37, 39, 41 -- the income test`

-- Limits of 200000 and 400000 are HYPOTHETICAL indexed amounts. A partnered claimant within the individual limit passes alone.
#ASSERT `Do I satisfy the income test` 120000 TRUE 300000 200000 400000
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I satisfy the income test` 250000 TRUE 200000 200000 400000)

-- c061: Chloe claims on 22 Aug 2030, before Oliver's birth: the income year ended 30 June 2030.
#ASSERT `My reference income year ended on 30 June of` 20300822 20300905 EQUALS 2030

