§ `ss 71A, 101 -- will my employer pay me`

-- c061: Ironbark pays Chloe. c063: Liam's 20 days cannot be a continuous flexible period, so even an electing employer
-- does not pay him. d04c: Jarrah cannot be Chloe's paymaster for Ella in April 2034, with or without an election.
#ASSERT `Can my run be a continuous flexible period` 20300905 20300905 110
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my run be a continuous flexible period` 20330412 20340414 40)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my run be a continuous flexible period` 20300905 20300905 20)

#ASSERT `Will my employer pay me` `Chloe at Ironbark for Oliver`
#ASSERT NOT (`Will my employer pay me` `Chloe at Jarrah for Ella in April 2034`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Will my employer pay me` `Chloe at Jarrah for Ella, Jarrah having elected`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Will my employer pay me` `Liam taking 20 days, his employer having elected`)

§ `ss 70-74, 80, 84, 99 -- who pays me, and what my employer must do`

-- k053: Jake has no employer; c063: Liam has no employer determination. The Secretary pays both.
#ASSERT `Who pays me for the day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my employer`
#ASSERT `Who pays me for the day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Secretary`

#ASSERT NOT (`Has my employer been paid enough` 4000 3000 1900 0)

#ASSERT `Must my employer pay me on my payday` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT (`May my employer pay me this way` `a set-off against a debt I owe my employer`)

#ASSERT NOT (`May my employer deduct it` `a debt I owe my employer`)

#ASSERT `By how many working days must my employer give me a record` TRUE EQUALS 1

#ASSERT NOT (`Does my unpaid leave become paid leave` TRUE)

§ `ss 115B, 115C; PPL rules s 36 -- superannuation`

-- PPL rules s 36 example: 305 elapsed days gives 0.0836. Base 10000, charge percentage 12 (HYPOTHETICAL here):
-- 1200 + 1200 x 0.0836 = 1300.32.
#ASSERT `What is my nominal interest multiplier` 305 EQUALS 0.0836

#ASSERT `How much superannuation contribution is paid for me` 10000 12 305 EQUALS 1300.32

